european union leaders have invited  croatia to the table as the country  prepares to become the eu's  28th member state on july 1.  this morning i should like to extend  a special welcome to our colleague  zoran milanovic prime minister  of croatia  accession will see the end of customs  controls at croatia's borders with eu  counterparts hungary and slovenia  easing trade business and travel while  it will not join the schengen  passport-free area  croat workers and services will be able  to move more smoothly throughout the eu  and vice versa the country will also  have access to funds for infrastructure  agriculture businesses education and to  help reduce  poverty elsewhere in the balkans serbia  and kosovo have taken major steps  forward in their quest for eu membership  following a vast improvement in  relations brokered by their two prime  ministers  eu leaders have decided to open  accession negotiations with serbia by  january at the latest  they also endorsed the launch of talks  with kosovo on a stabilization  and association agreement which could  pave the way for membership  in the future
 

